.TH SUPERSWITCHER 1 "" "superswitcher" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
superswitcher \- window and workspace switching using the Super key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B superswitcher
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SuperSwitcher replaces the Alt-Tab window switching and the
Ctrl-Alt-arrow workspace switching of a desktop.
While the program runs, holding the Super key shows a popup with the
workspaces and their windows.
Typing filters the windows by name, the arrow keys and the mouse activate
a window, and the function keys move to a workspace.
.PP
The program works only on X11, and exits in a Wayland session.
Only one instance runs at a time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-also\-trigger\-on\-caps\-lock
Make the Caps Lock key also switch windows, as well as the Super key.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-only\-trigger\-on\-caps\-lock
Make only the Caps Lock key switch windows, instead of the Super key.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-show\-window\-thumbnails
Experimental: show window thumbnails instead of icons.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help options and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Another instance is already running.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command-line option.
.TP
.B 3
This is a Wayland session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/SuperSwitcher.desktop
Starts the program in the graphical sessions of all users.
See
.I /usr/share/doc/superswitcher/README.Debian
to disable it.
